{
  "description": "firstRunIdleVpns / first_run_idle_vpns: once a VPN program is found on the machine, the additional-connection step offers its adapters that are down without the 'show unavailable' box. Adapters tied by a word (or by the interface the program names) to a found program; else the untied ones, named by the program when only one was found. A copy of a driver with other copies beside it (any state, among adapters the additional route may take) is never offered: the VPN brings up whichever copy it likes, so its program goes to `startVpnFirst` instead, unless a copy is up already or the program names that link. Nothing is picked unless the candidate is the one down VPN adapter on the machine (or the link a program names): a VPN client brings up whichever adapter it likes, of any driver, so among several the programs they may belong to go to `startVpnFirst`. `rows` are patches over `base-row`, `programs` are found programs, `skip` the main connection's pick; `expected.rows` lists `{index, program}`, `preselect` -1 for none.",
